WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.063 --> 00:00:10.670
During August, Pollyanna often visited Mr. Pendleton, but she wasn't sure how much her visits helped him.

2
00:00:10.671 --> 00:00:16.998
"He seems to like to hear me talk," she thought one afternoon as she walked home through Pendleton Woods.

3
00:00:16.999 --> 00:00:22.429
She smiled. "And I do like to talk!"

4
00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:26.518
But she had trouble predicting which topics would upset him.

5
00:00:26.519 --> 00:00:34.243
Today she had tried to tell him about the Glad Game, but he cut her off when she mentioned her father.

6
00:00:34.244 --> 00:00:41.229
Pollyanna remembered Nancy's idea that Mr. Pendleton and Aunt Polly had been engaged.

7
00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:44.502
"I'm beginning to think Nancy was right.

8
00:00:44.503 --> 00:00:51.345
Sometimes he's interested in what I say about Aunt Polly; other times he gets irritable.

9
00:00:51.346 --> 00:00:57.980
But he always listens with a strange smile on his face."

10
00:00:57.981 --> 00:01:02.764
Pollyanna stopped to watch two squirrels chasing each other.

11
00:01:02.765 --> 00:01:08.132
"Oh, I wish I could bring Aunt Polly and Mr. Pendleton together!

12
00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:12.991
They're both so lonely, but I don't know how to help them.

13
00:01:12.992 --> 00:01:17.152
Aunt Polly never wants to hear what I have to say about him.

14
00:01:17.153 --> 00:01:21.594
Then again, she never wants to hear about Dr. Chilton either.

15
00:01:21.595 --> 00:01:28.962
But that's probably because he saw her dressed up with the rose and shawl." ***

16
00:01:28.963 --> 00:01:34.192
Later that week Pollyanna again noticed Aunt Polly's dislike of Dr. Chilton.

17
00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:38.623
Pollyanna was in bed with a bad cold.

18
00:01:38.624 --> 00:01:44.126
"If you aren't better by tonight, I'm sending for the doctor," Aunt Polly said.

19
00:01:44.127 --> 00:01:52.975
"Then I hope I get worse." Pollyanna giggled. "I'd love to have Dr. Chilton visit."

20
00:01:52.976 --> 00:02:01.640
"Dr. Chilton is not our family physician," Aunt Polly said firmly. "I'll ask Dr. Warren to come."

21
00:02:01.641 --> 00:02:06.169
"I like Dr. Warren, but I like Dr. Chilton better.

22
00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:09.930
And Dr. Chilton would feel hurt if I didn't use him.

23
00:02:09.931 --> 00:02:14.559
It wasn't his fault that he saw you looking so pretty."

24
00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:21.739
"That will do, Pollyanna. I do not wish to discuss Dr. Chilton or his feelings."

25
00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:28.998
Pollyanna studied her aunt's face. "I'd love to fix your hair again, Aunt Polly. Wait—"

26
00:02:28.999 --> 00:02:33.583
But Aunt Polly had already left Pollyanna's room.

27
00:02:33.584 --> 00:02:38.707
That evening there was no need to summon a doctor.

28
00:02:38.708 --> 00:02:44.559
*** After Pollyanna had recovered, she paid another visit to Mr.

29
00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:52.137
Pendleton. Upon entering his room, she cried, "There's a rainbow on your

30
00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:55.052
pillow! How did it get inside the

31
00:02:55.053 --> 00:03:01.606
house?" "Do you see that thermometer hanging outside the window?" Mr. Pendleton

32
00:03:01.607 --> 00:03:06.638
pointed. "Sunlight striking its glass edge causes a prism

33
00:03:06.639 --> 00:03:12.730
effect." "Oh, that's so beautiful! I wish I could live in a

34
00:03:12.731 --> 00:03:19.717
rainbow." Mr. Pendleton laughed as he watched Pollyanna happily studying the

35
00:03:19.718 --> 00:03:22.794
colors. "Let's see what we can do about

36
00:03:22.795 --> 00:03:26.759
that." He touched a bell beside his bed, and the maid soon

37
00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:33.220
appeared. "Bring me a brass candlestick from the drawing room

38
00:03:33.221 --> 00:03:37.535
mantel." As the maid returned, Pollyanna heard

39
00:03:37.536 --> 00:03:42.073
tinkling. She noticed glass pendants hanging from the

40
00:03:42.074 --> 00:03:47.770
candlestick. "Oh, those pendants are making such a pretty musical

41
00:03:47.771 --> 00:03:55.810
sound!" Mr. Pendleton asked the maid to remove a curtain and stretch a string across the

42
00:03:55.811 --> 00:04:03.250
window. Then he slipped a dozen pendants from the

43
00:04:03.251 --> 00:04:07.205
candlestick. "Now, Pollyanna, hook these glass pieces onto the

44
00:04:07.206 --> 00:04:13.779
string. If you really want to live in a rainbow, we'll make one for

45
00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:17.904
you." Pollyanna hung three pendants in the sunlit

46
00:04:17.905 --> 00:04:24.643
window. She was so excited that her hands trembled and she could barely finish the

47
00:04:24.644 --> 00:04:30.844
job. At last she stepped back to admire her work.

48
00:04:30.845 --> 00:04:34.832
"It's like a fairyland!" she cried.

49
00:04:34.833 --> 00:04:39.071
The entire room was aglow with shimmering bits of color.

50
00:04:39.072 --> 00:04:43.574
"Perhaps the sun is trying to play the game!

51
00:04:43.575 --> 00:04:49.659
Oh, I wish I had prisms to give to Mrs. Snow and lots of folks.

52
00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:52.231
Nancy's birthday is next week.

53
00:04:52.232 --> 00:04:56.836
And they'd make Aunt Polly so glad, she'd bang doors."

54
00:04:56.837 --> 00:05:05.178
Mr. Pendleton laughed. "It would take more than prisms to make your aunt do that.

55
00:05:05.179 --> 00:05:08.098
But what is this game you mentioned?"

56
00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:13.673
Pollyanna explained the game and told him the story of the doll and crutches.

57
00:05:13.674 --> 00:05:16.527
This time he didn't mind hearing about her father.

58
00:05:16.528 --> 00:05:24.107
Tears came to his eyes. "I think you're the finest prism of all," he said.

59
00:05:24.108 --> 00:05:28.121
"No, beautiful colors don't shine through me.

60
00:05:28.122 --> 00:05:32.924
The sun just gives me freckles."

61
00:05:32.925 --> 00:05:38.042
Mr. Pendleton laughed, but Pollyanna thought it sounded more like a sob.

62
00:05:38.043 --> 00:05:41.528
He pressed the bell to summon the maid again.

63
00:05:41.529 --> 00:05:45.986
"Pollyanna, I'm sending you home with prisms for you and your friends.

64
00:05:45.987 --> 00:05:49.476
And a gold coin for Nancy's birthday."

65
00:05:49.477 --> 00:05:54.922
"Oh, thank you, sir!"

